    {
        "publicationNumber": "10127",
        "doi": "10.1049/ic:20040547",
        "publicationYear": "2004",
        "publicationDate": "3-3 Nov. 2004",
        "articleNumber": "1514241",
        "articleTitle": "The TV-Anytime forum's work",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "1",
        "endPage": "9",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "The IEE Storage and Home Networks Seminar, 2004.",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "S. Parnall",
                "firstName": "S.",
                "lastName": "Parnall"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "A nonprofit association of organisations which seeks to develop specifications to enable audio-visual services based on persistent local storage, with the deliberate policy to be platform 'agonstic' and produce specification that could be introduced to all digital platforms, in all three major market areas (Europe, USA and Asia). TVAF works in 2 phases. Phase one specifies benefit devices, which have hard-disc technology namely content referencing for acquisition, metadata for search and selection, metadata for segmentation/micronavigation and rights management information. Phase two add content packaging and management, advertising and interstitial support and rightful sharing.",
        "keywords": {
            "Index Terms": [
                "Metadata"
            ]
        }
    },
    {
        "publicationNumber": "10127",
        "doi": "10.1049/ic:20040549",
        "publicationYear": "2004",
        "publicationDate": "3-3 Nov. 2004",
        "articleNumber": "1514277",
        "articleTitle": "The emergence of PVR technology TV Anytime services. The DTG TV Anytime test bed",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "21",
        "endPage": "31",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "The IEE Storage and Home Networks Seminar, 2004.",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "A. Mornington-West",
                "firstName": "A.",
                "lastName": "Mornington-West"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The DTG TV Anytime test bed is the world's first test bed on an open free to air platform. Its target is to find out what it work, for whom and how. The TV Anytime is a service, which enabled powerful methods of managing a wide range of content. TV Anytime test bed objective establish the most effective use of TV Anytime methods in a UK DTT environment. It develops an appropriate test suite so that service providers can produce interoperable information.",
        "keywords": {}
    },
    {
        "publicationNumber": "10127",
        "doi": "10.1049/ic:20040551",
        "publicationYear": "2004",
        "publicationDate": "3-3 Nov. 2004",
        "articleNumber": "1514281",
        "articleTitle": "Building products with TV-Anytime: today and in the future",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "41",
        "endPage": "107",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "The IEE Storage and Home Networks Seminar, 2004.",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "M. Stuart",
                "firstName": "M.",
                "lastName": "Stuart"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "We describe the overview of how we are applying TV-Anytime to applications today and some emerging opportunities and new directions where TV-Anytime can thrive. TV-Anytime applications are (i) infrastructure and environment. (ii) Baseline set of applications.",
        "keywords": {
            "Index Terms": [
